goal:
Build a self-contained browser game using only HTML, CSS, and JavaScript.

Game: Frontier Trading Company

Requirements:

Single HTML file.
No external libraries.
No placeholders, TODOs, stubs, or pseudocode.
Must run immediately when opened in a browser.

Systems:

Economy

5 towns with different supply and demand.
Prices fluctuate daily.
Each town specializes in certain goods.

Trading

Player starts with $500 and a wagon.
Buy and sell goods.
Cargo capacity limits.
Profit/loss tracking.

Time

Days advance when traveling.
Traveling between towns consumes time.
Economy updates every day.

Events

Random events while traveling.
Examples: bandits, broken wheel, lucky merchant, market boom, market crash.
Events must have actual gameplay effects.

Player Progression

Wagon upgrades.
Increased cargo capacity.
Reduced travel costs.
Better trading efficiency.

UI

Town view.
Market view.
Travel controls.
Event log.
Statistics panel.

Save System

Save automatically to localStorage.
Load automatically on startup.

Architecture

Separate classes for:
Economy
Town
Player
Market
EventSystem
Game

Code Quality

No global state except the game bootstrap.
Use composition instead of one giant god object.
Include self-check assertions for critical calculations.
Avoid duplicate logic.
Keep systems loosely coupled.

At the end of the file include a brief comment explaining:

How the systems interact.
Why the architecture was chosen.
Which class owns which responsibilities.

